From: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] azidentity: avoid archive-incompatible test proxy setup

The upstream TestMain starts the Azure test proxy by locating the git
repository root and its development certificate. Release archive builds have
neither. Initialize the fake test values and run the tests directly instead;
environment-sensitive failures are still tolerated by the spec after a strict
compile pass.
---
 sdk/azidentity/live_test.go | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sdk/azidentity/live_test.go
+++ b/sdk/azidentity/live_test.go
@@ -123,5 +123,6 @@

 func TestMain(m *testing.M) {
-	code := run(m)
+	setFakeValues()
+	code := m.Run()
 	os.Exit(code)
 }
